  "body": "Found while fixing #67. Cross drill reads its standoff/hop radius from the part's facets, not the setup's stock. A cross drill run before the bar is turned to size (stock radius > part radius) would hop between stations inside the raw stock - a rapid through material.\n\nFirst check whether the rapid-in-stock verification (crates/sim verify, rapids_in_stock) catches it and blocks the post; if it does not, this is a P0 (collision) and must be raised.\n\nDone means: cross drill measures its standoff/clearance about the larger of the stock and the part (at the station), with a test where the stock is wider than the finished bar; or the post is refused by name when the hop would cut stock.",
